-- issue #1382 repro A, verbatim from the issue body. `armod` declares a record
-- TYPE named `Cfg` with fields `a` then `b`. main.mdk never imports `Cfg` from
-- here -- only the unrelated `arSum` -- but this module's `Cfg` is still
-- visible to the native emitter's program-global record layout via the module
-- graph, because `zrmod.mdk` declares another `Cfg` with a DIFFERENT field
-- order (see zrmod.mdk).
--
-- ⚠️ The module NAME "armod" is load-bearing: which module's layout wins is
-- decided by module-name SORT ORDER, not import-clause order (per the issue).
-- Renaming this file changes which projection ends up wrong. Do not rename.
public export data Cfg = { a : Int, b : Int }
mkA : Cfg
mkA = Cfg { a = 11, b = 22 }
export arSum : Int
arSum = mkA.a + mkA.b
